<title>GERMANY: Hoechst, Dow to build acrylic acid plant.</title>
<headline>Hoechst, Dow to build acrylic acid plant.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemical and pharmaceutical group Hoechst AG said on Tuesday it had an agreement to build an acrylic acid plant in Germany with Dow Chemical Co with a capacity of 80,000 tonnes.  </p>
<p>The new plant, to be based in Schkopau, east Germany, will develop raw acrylic acid, which will then be used in the manufacture of other products. Production is due to start in 1999.</p>
<p>Buna Sow Leuna Olefinverbund  BSL will also participate in the project, which was described in Hoechst's statement as &quot;key&quot; to BSL's plans for privatisation. No details were given of the cost of the plant.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
